WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.330
- I'm an American in
every sense of the word,

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:03.651
I know Cardi B.
- Yeah.

00:00:03.651 --> 00:00:05.695
(laughs)

00:00:05.695 --> 00:00:08.278
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.210
In what country is this possible?

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.670
You come from Africa and
you're in Hollywood now.

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:18.183
All my life I've kinda like,
hidden my immigration status,

00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:21.540
and it wasn't until they
decided to cancel it that

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.910
I was like, look, I
can't be scared anymore.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:26.290
I can't hide in the shadows anymore.

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:29.930
I'm in Black Panther, I'm in
The Good Place and I feel like,

00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:33.187
to whom much is given, much
is expected or required.

00:00:33.187 --> 00:00:34.860
- Yeah.
- So, I decided to

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.970
use my voice and to amplify the message

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.900
and to actually put a face to the, to this

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:43.760
real political issue.
- Yeah.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.290
- That a lot of people don't
understand or know about.

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.130
I'm a dreamer, meaning
I'm a DACA recipient.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.830
This is Deferred Action
for Childhood Arrivals that

00:00:51.830 --> 00:00:55.250
Obama signed as an
executive order in 2012, and

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.723
Trump Administration decided
to cancel it back in September.

00:01:02.612 --> 00:01:07.024
- [Chanting Protesters] The
whole world is watching!

00:01:07.024 --> 00:01:08.860
The whole world is watching!

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:13.860
- There's not a day that
undocumented people go without

00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:17.700
a thought of possibly being
torn away from everything that

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:20.140
they love, from their
family, from the life that

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:21.970
they've built here because of

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:24.170
sometimes, just a minor technicality.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:26.580
You don't renew your visa and all of a

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.160
sudden, you're rendered illegal.

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:32.110
You can't adjust your
status to anything else.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:34.920
Like, I came here when I was
10 years old with my parents,

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:38.490
seeking political asylum,
fleeing war, and now,

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.830
I'm on DACA and I've been in this country

00:01:40.830 --> 00:01:43.150
25 years and my whole life, I just thought

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.550
I could achieve a lot of success.

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:47.980
I could just be great
at everything that I do.

00:01:47.980 --> 00:01:51.340
Try to be a model citizen,
give back to the community and

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:53.720
then eventually, the thing
would work, there just

00:01:53.720 --> 00:01:57.390
seems like there's no door,
there's no way to actually

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:59.310
adjust the status, I've tried everything.

00:01:59.310 --> 00:02:00.850
People are like, well, you didn't do this.

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:03.130
No, I've seen as many lawyers as possible.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:06.790
I'm doing everything that you
can humanly do just so that

00:02:06.790 --> 00:02:09.150
I can have the peace
of mind that, you know,

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:12.160
I'm gonna be okay and my
family won't be torn apart.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.980
We're not murderers or killers, we're not

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.710
trying to take away from
America, we love America.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:19.980
We just want an opportunity
to have a permanent solution.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:23.403
We want Congress to
finally pass a Dream Act.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.880
America's at a crossroad,
and Americans have a

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:33.650
decision to make as far as like,

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.720
what country does America wanna be?

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:40.073
Americans have been able
to break walls of race,

00:02:40.073 --> 00:02:44.450
of gender inequality, of
disability, of just so many

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:46.800
amazing things which
makes this country great.

00:02:46.800 --> 00:02:49.010
That's, that's the America that I love and

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:51.623
I believe and I want to remain in.

00:02:52.606 --> 00:02:55.273
(mellow music)

